Deliberate divergences from upstream v0.1.0
-------------------------------------------
- Response token counter: local UTF-8 byte estimator (utf8-bytes@1/ceil-4),
  not tiktoken cl100k_base. Tracks cl100k closely on code/JSON; batch packing
  still keeps 30% headroom. Counter id is reported in every result.
- JS/TS syntax chunker dropped (upstream pins a TypeScript compiler). Line
  windows are the only strategy; chunker id jevgrep-py-line-windows-1. Cache
  identities therefore never collide with upstream entries.
- Vercel AI Gateway adapter speaks the gateway evaluation-model HTTP contract
  directly (spec header v4) instead of the upstream AI SDK wrapper.
- Windows reparse-point attribute checks are simplified to lstat/realpath
  containment. No junction-specific probing. Symlinked ancestors above the
  authorized root are tolerated (macOS /tmp, /var); links inside the root stay
  refused.
- Trusted configuration file is YAML, parsed with sage.jev.yaml_lite. Field
  names match the upstream configuration contract.
- Score cache schema_version 3 with upstream identity inputs, but canonical
  JSON encoding details differ: upstream and port caches do not interoperate
  (they are separate directories anyway).
- Response contract (schema_version "1") shape and validator invariants are
  ported as-is.

Unchanged by design: per-repository remote-evaluation opt-in, credential
pattern quarantine, no-redirect bounded HTTP, strict answer validation
(unavailable evaluation is never a zero score), deterministic batching and
selection, freshness revalidation before rendering, one active + one queued
MCP search then BUSY.
